####  Using a binding pattern as the rest property

The rest property of array destructuring assignment can be another array or
object binding pattern. The inner destructuring destructures from the array
created after collecting the rest elements, so you cannot access any
properties present on the original iterable in this way.

js



    const [a, b, ...{ length }] = [1, 2, 3];
    console.log(a, b, length); // 1 2 1


js



    const [a, b, ...[c, d]] = [1, 2, 3, 4];
    console.log(a, b, c, d); // 1 2 3 4


