####  pub fn  insert  (&mut self, k: K, v: V) -> [ Option
](../option/enum.Option.html "enum std::option::Option") <V>

Inserts a key-value pair into the map.

If the map did not have this key present, [ ` None `
](../option/enum.Option.html#variant.None "variant std::option::Option::None")
is returned.

If the map did have this key present, the value is updated, and the old value
is returned. The key is not updated, though; this matters for types that can
be ` == ` without being identical. See the [ module-level documentation
](index.html#insert-and-complex-keys "mod std::collections") for more.

#####  Â§  Examples



    use std::collections::HashMap;

    let mut map = HashMap::new();
    assert_eq!(map.insert(37, "a"), None);
    assert_eq!(map.is_empty(), false);

    map.insert(37, "b");
    assert_eq!(map.insert(37, "c"), Some("b"));
    assert_eq!(map[&37], "c");

