If  V  models [ ` input_range ` ](/w/cpp/ranges/input_range "cpp/ranges/input
range") (1)  , ` chunk_view ` 's iterator has a dedicated type: [ `
_outer_iterator::value_type_ `
](/w/cpp/ranges/chunk_view/outer_iterator/value_type "cpp/ranges/chunk
view/outer iterator/value type") that is itself an input view.

If  V  models [ ` forward_range ` ](/w/cpp/ranges/forward_range
"cpp/ranges/forward range") or stronger  (2)  , ` chunk_view ` defers to
views::take  for its ` value_type ` .

If  V  models [ ` bidirectional_range ` ](/w/cpp/ranges/bidirectional_range
"cpp/ranges/bidirectional range") or stronger ranges  (2)  , the need to
calculate size the last chunk correctly (from the end [ iterator
](/w/cpp/ranges/chunk_view/iterator "cpp/ranges/chunk view/iterator") )
requires the underlying range type  V  to be [ ` sized_range `
](/w/cpp/ranges/sized_range "cpp/ranges/sized range") .

